    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with an emphasis on capitalizing on soft matchups to chase stolen bases and volume. The trio of **James Wood** (76.28), **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.99) represent our strongest offensive engine today. **James Wood** is the premier play, leveraging an elite xwOBA of 0.428 and a favorable matchup against Michael Lorenzen. His #1 spot in the order, combined with wind-out conditions, creates a high ceiling for run production. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against Miles Mikolas; despite a 33% rain risk, his speed profile and projected slotting make him a core component of today's strategy. **Vinnie Pasquantino** rounds out our top-tier trio, taking advantage of a dynamic platoon edge against Tyler Mahle, which provides a significant boost to his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench involves **Austin Riley**, who scored a respectable 62.89 but ultimately fell short of the starting cut. While **Austin Riley** offers pedigree and a positive matchup against Walker Buehler, the optimizer prioritized the speed-weighted efficiency of **Jose Caballero** and **Brice Turang**, whose ability to potentially generate stolen bases against softer pitchers like Bubba Chandler and Zac Thornton carries more weight in our current Roto standings. We are also keeping a close eye on the weather; while **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, **James Wood**, and **Kyle Karros** are all in the starting lineup, the combined 33\u201341% rain risk across their respective venues introduces volatility. If any of these games are postponed, expect to see pivots toward bench options like **Josh Naylor**, who offers a high floor if the primary weather risks manifest.",
